# Tier III (dav1d's terminology, see package/multimedia/dav1d/ia64-simd.patch)
# kernels for SWGL's YUV -> BGRA video rows, in the same style as
# hotfix-swgl-ia64-tier3-r8-kernels.patch: a generated, modulo-scheduled
# assembly file with its own register frame. Two entry points:
#
#   swgl_yuv42_row_ia64         upscaleYUV42R8, 4:2:0 at <= 1 luma texel/px
#   swgl_yuv42_row_linear_ia64  linear_row_yuv's generic R8 loop (any scale:
#                               downscaled video, and the edge chunks of the
#                               upscale path)
#
# The C upscale loop repairs a sliding window with lane shuffles that GCC
# lowers to serial extr/dep chains, 127 bundles per four pixels; the kernels
# gather the taps instead, under index rules that reproduce the shuffles (and
# the generic loop's edge clamps) exactly - checked against the C on random
# spans before any assembly was written. Positions advance as 32-bit lane
# pairs, row 1 is loaded through ld1's register post-increment, and the
# registers are allocated by packing lifetimes on the rotating file.
#
# On a browsing session (news, Discord, YouTube) linear_row_yuv was 2.7% of
# all CPU cycles, 19% of the SWGL thread. Itanium 2 (Montecito), cycles per
# pixel, byte-identical output, CompositeYUV of 4:2:0 R8 planes into
# 1024x768; x86-64 is the same benchmark on a Ryzen 5900HX:
#                                          C path   Tier III   x86-64
#   YUV 4:2:0 1:1                           45.7      11.7      46.8
#   YUV 4:2:0 upscale (640x360)             45.5      11.6      46.8
#   YUV 4:2:0 downscale (1920x1080)         97.1      14.9     109.5
#
# The upscale kernel needs a minimum step (an upscale below ~16000x) for one
# of its index rules; the caller checks it and otherwise keeps the C loop.

